Description: Check a group that lists no members by name
 pam_group skipped a group whose member list was empty. A user can still be
 a member by primary group, by UUID or through a nested group. So a deny
 rule for such a group let its members in. FreeBSD's pam_group dropped the
 same check in 2014. The manual page no longer says that fail_safe admits
 the applicant to an existing group with no members.
Origin: backport, https://github.com/freebsd/freebsd-src/commit/ec5622ad86451436339a2dc2c15213956d73adc8
Author: The Blueberry Pie OS Authors
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-17

--- a/modules/pam_group/pam_group.c
+++ b/modules/pam_group/pam_group.c
@@ -32,6 +32,9 @@
  * OUT OF THE USE OF THIS SOFTWARE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF
  * SUCH DAMAGE.
  */
+/*
+ * Modified 2026-11-17: a group that lists no members by name is checked like any other group.
+ */
 
 #include <sys/cdefs.h>
 
@@ -111,10 +114,6 @@ pam_sm_acct_mgmt(pam_handle_t *pamh, int
 		if ((grp = getgrnam(p)) == NULL || grp->gr_mem == NULL)
 			continue;
 
-		/* check if the group is empty */
-		if (*grp->gr_mem == NULL)
-			continue;
-
 		found_group = 1;
 
 		/* check membership */
--- a/modules/pam_group/pam_group.8
+++ b/modules/pam_group/pam_group.8
@@ -35,7 +35,8 @@
 .\"
 .\" Protions copyright (c) 2009 Apple Inc. All rights reserved.
 .\"
-.Dd February 7, 2009
+.\" Modified 2026-11-17: fail_safe applies only when none of the groups exists.
+.Dd November 17, 2026
 .Dt pam_group 8
 .Os
 .Sh NAME
@@ -67,7 +68,7 @@ The following options may be passed to t
 .It Cm deny
 Reverse the meaning of the test, i.e., reject the applicant if and only if he or she is a member of the specified group.  This can be useful to exclude certain groups of users from certain services.
 .It Cm fail_safe
-If the specified group does not exist, or has no members, act as if it does exist and the applicant is a member.
+If none of the specified groups exists, act as if the applicant is a member.
 .It Cm group=groupname
 Specify the name of the group to check.  This can be a comma-separated list 
 .Pq i.e. Dq group=admin,wheel .
